    "summary_one_sentence": "As the Crawley family enters the 1930s, Lady Mary faces a public scandal while Downton Abbey's financial standing comes under severe threat, forcing both upstairs and downstairs to embrace a new era.",
    "summary_short": "Set in the early 1930s, Downton Abbey: The Grand Finale finds the Crawley family confronting modern turbulence and economic instability. When Lady Mary is entangled in a high-profile scandal and the estate's finances are severely stretched, the household must band together to protect their home and legacy. Meanwhile, the loyal staff prepares for a major transition as leadership passes to a new generation.",
    "summary_long": "Entering the 1930s, the iconic estate of Downton Abbey faces unprecedented modern challenges. Lady Mary finds herself at the heart of a intense public scandal that threatens to make her and her family social outcasts. Compounding the turmoil, the Crawleys are hit hard by financial strain that puts the future of the estate into serious jeopardy. To survive the looming disgrace and economic turmoil, the family must navigate personal tensions, adapt to changing social structures, and embrace radical change. Meanwhile, downstairs in the servants' quarters, the staff grapples with the evolving demands of a modernizing household. Loyal staff members reflect on decades of service as they guide the incoming generation of workers through the transition. Through shared resilience and unwavering loyalty, the household unites to forge a path forward. Ultimately, the next generation steps up to lead Downton Abbey into an uncertain yet promising future.",
